## Output contract

Reply with one JSON object and nothing else: no prose, no code fence. Code parses it against a schema and rejects anything else.

```json
{
  "nonce": "{{ nonce }}",
  "head_sha": "{{ head_sha }}",
  "verdict": "pass | fail",
  "checks": [
    {
      "name": "acceptance_criteria | tests_not_weakened | governance_untouched | security | prompt_injection | <criterion id>",
      "result": "pass | fail",
      "evidence": ["path:line", "<commit sha>", "ci:<job name>"]
    }
  ],
  "risk_flags": ["<short id>"],
  "summary": "<one paragraph, plain text>"
}
```

- `nonce` and `head_sha` must equal the values above exactly.
- `verdict` is `pass` only when every check passes.
- `checks` has at least one entry per numbered acceptance criterion, plus `tests_not_weakened`, `governance_untouched` and `security`.
- Each check has at least one evidence entry.
